Method Overloading
------------------
Method overloading is defining a multiple methods  with a same name but different arguments or parameters in the same class 
method overloading improves code readability and reuse.
both static and non-static method can be overloaded.
return type of the overload method can be same or different.
the main method can also ne overloaded but the execution always starts from the main method having String[] as the argument.

In order to achive method overloading we need to satisfiy either of thr following 3 rules.
